# s3-06: fill_saved_login served by the core (SavedLoginComputerBackend)

[mixdog-core-session/src/session/secret_input.rs] (not a hot file, but not owned by s3-06 either)
After `pub use computer::HostComputerCommands;` add:
    pub use computer::SavedLoginComputerBackend;
    pub use computer::SavedLoginTurns;

[mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs] in the `computer_pool` session closure (the one that builds
`RedactingComputerBackend` then `GatedComputerBackend`), wrap the gated backend:
    let gated = GatedComputerBackend::new(redacted, human_only.clone());
    Arc::new(SavedLoginComputerBackend::new(
        Arc::new(gated),
        ThreadId::from(session),
        <desktop browser host: mixdog_tools::desktop::host::ChannelHostCommands::new(b.host.clone()) (no redaction needed: the vault answer is consumed by the fill)>,
        Arc::new(HostComputerCommands::new(late_computer_hosts.clone(), human_only.clone())),
        <ONE Arc<SavedLoginRegistry> = SavedLoginRegistry::new(), created beside `fill`>,
        <redactor: Arc<FullRedactor { saved: registry.clone(), sessions: fill.clone() }> in place of `fill.clone()` for RedactingComputerBackend too, so saved-login passwords are hidden from every computer reply>,
        <Arc<dyn SavedLoginTurns>: the number of the session's running agent turn (1-based, Node's turn_id), None when none runs>,
    ))
and create the registry/redactor before `computer_pool` (the redactor replaces `fill.clone()` in RedactingComputerBackend::new and in the `fill` handoff env where it hides replies).

[turn settlement] the owner of the agent turn calls `registry.settle(&SavedLoginTurn { session, turn }).await` when a turn settles and `registry.forget(session).await` when a session ends (lifts the password redaction and the pixel guard); no code calls these yet.

[SERVICE_PENDING] nothing to remove: fill_saved_login is a computer action, not a protocol method; `host/browser/command` saved_login_* already exists.
